  "pages": [
    {
      "page_idx": 8,
      "blocks": [
        {
          "type": "header",
          "index": 0,
          "bbox": [
            0.736,
            0.047,
            0.847,
            0.063
          ],
          "content": [
            {
              "type": "text",
              "content": "Number Play"
            }
          ]
        },
        {
          "type": "text",
          "index": 1,
          "bbox": [
            0.149,
            0.088,
            0.848,
            0.162
          ],
          "content": [
            {
              "type": "text",
              "content": "Let us focus, for the moment, only on the row sums. We have seen that in a 3 × 3 grid with numbers 1 – 9, the total of row sums will always be 45. Since in a magic square the row sums are all equal, and they add up to 45, they have to be 15 each. Thus, we have the following observation."
            }
          ]
        },
        {
          "type": "text",
          "index": 2,
          "bbox": [
            0.149,
            0.162,
            0.847,
            0.2
          ],
          "content": [
            {
              "type": "text",
              "content": "Observation 1:",
              "styles": [
                "bold"
              ]
            },
            {
              "type": "text",
              "content": " In a magic square made using the numbers 1 – 9, the magic sum must be 15."
            }
          ]
        },
        {
          "type": "text",
          "index": 3,
          "bbox": [
            0.161,
            0.204,
            0.846,
            0.241
          ],
          "content": [
            {
              "type": "text",
              "content": "2. What are the possible numbers that could occur at the centre of a magic square?"
            }
          ]
        },
        {
          "type": "text",
          "index": 4,
          "bbox": [
            0.15,
            0.241,
            0.627,
            0.296
          ],
          "content": [
            {
              "type": "text",
              "content": "Let us consider the possibilities one by one. Can the central number be 9? If yes, then 8 must come in one of the other squares. For example,"
            }
          ]
        },
        {
          "type": "text",
          "index": 5,
          "bbox": [
            0.151,
            0.297,
            0.627,
            0.351
          ],
          "content": [
            {
              "type": "text",
              "content": "In this, we must have 8 + 9 + other number = 15. But this is not possible! The same issue will occur no matter where we place 8."
            }
          ]
        },
        {
          "type": "text",
          "index": 6,
          "bbox": [
            0.15,
            0.352,
            0.627,
            0.387
          ],
          "content": [
            {
              "type": "text",
              "content": "So, 9 cannot be at the centre. Can the central number be 1?"
            }
          ]
        },
        {
          "type": "image",
          "index": 7,
          "bbox": [
            0.645,
            0.239,
            0.834,
            0.371
          ],
          "content": [
            {
              "type": "image_body",
              "index": 7,
              "bbox": [
                0.645,
                0.239,
                0.834,
                0.371
              ],
              "image_path": "images/page_8_image_7.jpg",
              "content": ""
            }
          ]
        },
        {
          "type": "text",
          "index": 8,
          "bbox": [
            0.15,
            0.388,
            0.629,
            0.425
          ],
          "content": [
            {
              "type": "text",
              "content": "If yes, then 2 should come in one of the other squares."
            }
          ]
        },
        {
          "type": "text",
          "index": 9,
          "bbox": [
            0.15,
            0.425,
            0.631,
            0.499
          ],
          "content": [
            {
              "type": "text",
              "content": "Here, we must have 2 + 1 + other number = 15. But this is not possible because we are only using the numbers 1 – 9. The same issue will occur no matter where we place 1."
            }
          ]
        },
        {
          "type": "text",
          "index": 10,
          "bbox": [
            0.174,
            0.499,
            0.532,
            0.517
          ],
          "content": [
            {
              "type": "text",
              "content": "So, 1 cannot be at the centre, either."
            }
          ]
        },
        {
          "type": "image",
          "index": 11,
          "bbox": [
            0.648,
            0.4,
            0.834,
            0.532
          ],
          "content": [
            {
              "type": "image_body",
              "index": 11,
              "bbox": [
                0.648,
                0.4,
                0.834,
                0.532
              ],
              "image_path": "images/page_8_image_11.jpg",
              "content": ""
            }
          ]
        },
        {
          "type": "text",
          "index": 12,
          "bbox": [
            0.111,
            0.526,
            0.628,
            0.566
          ],
          "content": [
            {
              "type": "text",
              "content": "Using such reasoning, find out which other numbers 1 – 9 cannot occur at the centre."
            }
          ]
        },
        {
          "type": "text",
          "index": 13,
          "bbox": [
            0.15,
            0.576,
            0.634,
            0.614
          ],
          "content": [
            {
              "type": "text",
              "content": "This exploration will lead us to the following interesting observation."
            }
          ]
        },
        {
          "type": "text",
          "index": 14,
          "bbox": [
            0.149,
            0.613,
            0.634,
            0.668
          ],
          "content": [
            {
              "type": "text",
              "content": "Observation 2:",
              "styles": [
                "bold"
              ]
            },
            {
              "type": "text",
              "content": " The number occurring at the centre of a magic square, filled using 1 – 9, must be 5."
            }
          ]
        },
        {
          "type": "footer",
          "index": 15,
          "bbox": [
            0.449,
            0.971,
            0.551,
            0.984
          ],
          "content": [
            {
              "type": "text",
              "content": "Reprint 2026-27"
            }
          ]
        },
        {
          "type": "image",
          "index": 16,
          "bbox": [
            0.653,
            0.578,
            0.838,
            0.708
          ],
          "content": [
            {
              "type": "image_body",
              "index": 16,
              "bbox": [
                0.653,
                0.578,
                0.838,
                0.708
              ],
              "image_path": "images/page_8_image_16.jpg",
